'''''Scirpoides holoschoenus''''' is a species of perennial sedge in the family [[Cyperaceae]], commonly called the '''roundhead bulrush'''.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Scirpoides holoschoenus (L.) Soják |url=https://www.gbif.org/species/2718201 |access-date=2022-03-17 |website=www.gbif.org |language=en}}</ref> It has a self-supporting growth form and simple, broad leaves. They are associated with freshwater habitat. Individuals can grow to 0.75 m.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Scirpoides holoschoenus (L.) Soják - Encyclopedia of Life|url=https://eol.org/pages/249915|access-date=2022-02-04|website=eol.org}}</ref>

